{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Let's find the limit as $x$ approaches $1$. We will use the fact that $f(x)=\\text{ln}(x)$ for $x$-values larger than $0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 1}f(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\text{ln}(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\text{ln}(1)\u0026\\gray{\\text{Direct substitution}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=0\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, we found that $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$f(x)=\\begin{cases}\nx^2\u0026\\text{for }x\\leq0\n\\\\\\\\\n\\text{ln}(x)\u0026\\text{for }x\u003e0\n\\end{cases}$\n\n**Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 1}f(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$0$","correct":true},{"content":"$1$","correct":false},{"content":"$e$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"The limit doesn't exist.","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
